# MPPE imbuition review (eoschool drafting)

Use this rule when **reviewing** or **auditing** Homescool copy for MPPE Venezuela grade-3 coverage. Content master remains eoschool (`eoschool-mppe-master.mdc`).

## Review questions (every pass)

1. **Catalog completeness** — Does `mppe-grade3-checklist.json` still list every aprendizaje esperado from `marco_programatico_mppe_y_tercer_grado.md` Part II? If the marco gained items, update the catalog first.
2. **Claim vs evidence** — For each class with `mppe.objectives[]`, does the lesson/quiz **actually** practice that id (not only list it)?
3. **Orphan objectives** — Which checklist ids have **zero** class keys declaring them? Mark as gap; propose imbuition into an existing week theme or a **new** week theme.
4. **Over-claim** — Same id listed on many days without new practice? Prefer day-1 intro + deepen evidence, not copy-paste of the whole week list on every day unless each day truly reinforces it.
5. **Student visibility** — Is the label on the sheet explicit and readable? Missing `mppe` block on a class that clearly imbues MPPE = fail the review.
6. **Master integrity** — Did the edit keep METHOD_V1 structure and narrative spec 009 while imbuing?

## Pass / fail signals

| Signal | Pass | Fail |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Objective in catalog | Has stable `id` | Free-text only, no id |
| Class declaration | `mppe.objectives` with id+label | Imbuition in prose but no declaration |
| Coverage trend | Gaps shrink week over week | Permanent silent gaps in Ciencias/Identidad blocks |
| Theme master | Title/3 points intact | Theme replaced by MPPE syllabus dump |

## Review workflow for agents

1. Open checklist + curriculum (or cell JSON under `media/weekN/`).
2. Build a coverage table: `objectiveId → [class keys]`.
3. List **uncovered** ids grouped by area (mat / cie / ide / len).
4. For the files in scope, verify declaration ↔ body alignment.
5. Report: covered count / total, top gaps, concrete next imbuitions (class key + id + where in body).

## UI cross-check

After content changes, use the Homescool **MPPE checklist** modal (`fact_check` in DHS) to confirm the same coverage the agent computed. Do not treat the modal alone as authorization to skip reading lesson bodies.
